  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A lightweight in-browser alternative to Coot for viewing a PDB model together with its electron-density maps (its main purpose), rotating it and picking atoms, with a companion 3D viewer for reciprocal-space spot lists that shows which lattice each spot was indexed to. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
